/// known-gap: interp puts every modified field back to its value from before the overlay
/// When a timed overlay ends it takes back only what its `modifies:` added,
/// so other changes to the field meanwhile stay, and two overlays on one
/// field can end in either order.
<>F |
    hp: 20
    def: 2
xx
overlay Weak |
    lasts 3 ticks
    modifies:
        hp - 2
    end
end
overlay Shield |
    lasts 2 ticks
    modifies:
        def + 3
    end
end
overlay Blessed |
    lasts 4 ticks
    modifies:
        def + 1
    end
end
a <> F | hp: 20
overlay Weak on a at 1
overlay Shield on a at 1
overlay Blessed on a at 1
repeat :range(1, 6) as d
    a >> hp |= a >> hp - 1
    if d == 1
        a >> def |= a >> def + 10
    xx
    tick()
    h | a >> hp
    df | a >> def
    say("tick {d}: hp {h}, def {df}")
xx
